    If the data is missing: Our own information — establish it. Name the banker who would own the deal.
  "IB_DEAL_SIZE" - Deal Size (G.5)
    Definition: Capital being raised, in US$ Mn at the workbook FX rate. Scored against mandate economics — below the Fair cut the fee will not cover the effort.
    Where to look: The ask, from the deck or term sheet. Convert at ₹94 = US$1 (US$ Mn × 9.4 = INR Cr).
    Report "value" as a number in US$ Mn.
    Scored at Series A (higher is better): Excellent 15.0000, Good 8.0000, Fair 4.0000.
    If the data is missing: Sense-check against the sub-sector average ticket in F.3 — an ask far above sub-sector norms will be hard to place regardless of quality.

