### 1. What is the company overview of Zyla Health (https://zyla.in)? Give a detailed description of what the business does.

Zyla Health is an AI-powered personalized care management platform based in India, focused on revolutionizing healthcare delivery by improving health outcomes for individuals. The company provides a full spectrum of personalized health and wellness solutions that span both preventive and chronic health conditions. Zyla Health offers continuous, round-the-clock care through an in-house team of doctors and healthcare professionals, leveraging advanced human-assisted AI technology.

The platform assesses risk profiles, recommends health interventions, and implements them with precision, utilizing its proprietary deep-tech platform to analyze multiple data points from patient history and identify causality across various health conditions. Zyla Health's offerings include specialized programs for managing conditions such as heart health, blood pressure and cholesterol, chronic kidney diseases, liver diseases, women's health issues (PCOS, thyroid, osteoporosis, vitamin/mineral deficiency), pregnancy, and post-COVID recovery.

Zyla Health partners with leading insurance companies to help reduce hospitalizations and costs, collaborates with corporations to safeguard employee health and well-being, and works with pharmaceutical and e-pharma companies to enable care for patients at scale. The company aims to be the de-facto healthcare expert in every household, serving millions of users and addressing a vast number of simultaneous patient queries. The Zyla app is available for Android and iOS users and has reportedly touched over 150,000 patient lives across more than 595 cities in India (Source: YourStory, https://yourstory.com/companies/zyla-health).

### 2. What is the full legal/registered name of Zyla Health, and what brand names does it trade under?

The full legal/registered name of the company is Zyla Health Private Limited (Source: YourStory, https://yourstory.com/companies/zyla-health; Tracxn, https://tracxn.com/companies/zyla-health-private-limited/financials; ZaubaCorp, https://www.zaubacorp.com/company/ZYLA-HEALTH-PRIVATE-LIMITED/U86909DL2017PTC343630; Bloomberg LEI, https://www.bloomberg.com/profile/company/33580082T69PFJQWRC69). The company primarily trades under the brand name Zyla Health.

### 3. In which year was Zyla Health founded, and what is its founding history?

Zyla Health was founded in 2017 (Source: Zyla Health, https://zyla.in/about-us; Inc42, https://inc42.com/startup-masterclass/zyla-health-funding-revenue-investors; YourStory, https://yourstory.com/companies/zyla-health; Tracxn, https://tracxn.com/d/companies/zyla). The inspiration for Zyla Health originated from a personal experience of its founder and CEO, Khushboo Aggarwal, whose father suffered a cardiac event. This incident highlighted significant gaps in healthcare delivery in India, particularly the lack of continuous, round-the-clock care for chronic patients.

Aggarwal left her previous job to address this challenge, starting the journey from a one-room office in Delhi in 2017. Initially, Zyla Health focused on managing diabetes patients and later expanded its offerings to include a wide range of chronic conditions such as heart, liver, and kidney issues, blood pressure, cholesterol management, and women's health concerns. The company's mission evolved to focus on value-based care, leading to its current comprehensive care management platform.

